course: dictionary
lesson: 2302
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Crisp is one of them. Its meaning depends on what it describes. «The apples were crisp and sweet, so they crunched when we bit them.» Here crisp is about food that is fresh and hard, so it breaks with a crunch.
explain: The clues are in the rest of the sentence. Look at what the word is describing and what happens around it. «Ella's £2 crisps just fit» is about money and shopping, so crisps must be a packet snack, not something crunchy from a garden.
explain: Words can also change their job. Crisp can describe weather, paper or clothes, or the way someone speaks. In «a crisp autumn morning», crisp means cold, dry and fresh. A crisp way of speaking is quick and clear.
fact: «Crisp» means hard and dry in a nice way, so it breaks with a crunch.
fact: Crisp weather is cold, dry and fresh.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, crisps are thin fried potato slices in a packet. Americans call them chips.
fact: «British "crisps" are American "chips".»
fact: A crisp way of speaking is quick and clear.
exercise: «Ella's £2 crisps just fit in the shopping plan.» What are crisps here? | A quick, clear way of speaking | Cold, dry weather | A kind of bread | *Thin fried potato slices in a packet
exercise: «It was a crisp autumn morning, cold and clear.» What does crisp mean here? | Burnt and black | Loud and noisy | *Cold, dry and fresh | Soft and sticky
exercise: Grandad says «The toast is burnt to a crisp.» What does crisp mean in this sentence? | Soft and sticky | Quick and clear | Cold and fresh | *Hard, dry and burnt
test: Jayden says crisp is only a snack. Is he right? | Yes, crisp always means a packet snack | *No, crisp can also mean fresh and crunchy, cold and dry, or quick and clear | No, it always means soft and wet | No, but it always means cold weather
test: Which word in «Picture Saturday morning» is a packet snack? | £80 | spare | *crisps | shop
exam: In «British "crisps" are American "chips"», what are British crisps? | Cold, dry weather | Chopped fries for dinner | Quick, clear talk | *Thin fried potato slices in a packet
